From 60e08955fe23c2a1d57834f7dc31860395542e4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sorgelig <pour.garbage@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Jul 2021 16:39:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] hid-playstation: dualsense mic-mute as BTN_Z + userspace mute LED

Vanilla handles the DualSense mic-mute button entirely in-kernel: a
press toggles the hardware microphone and mute LED, invisible to
userspace. Stock MiSTer instead reports the button as BTN_Z -- giving
the controller one extra mappable input -- and exposes the mute LED as
a writable "<hid-dev>:mute" LED class device so userspace owns it. The
in-kernel toggle is removed (nothing on MiSTer records from the
controller microphone).

BTN_Z IS DUALSENSE-ONLY, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING
BTN_Z is 0x135, between BTN_WEST (0x134) and BTN_TL (0x136), so
declaring it shifts every higher gamepad button up one index in the
device's EV_KEY capability bitmap. Main_MiSTer derives SDL-style `bN`
indices by walking that bitmap --

    Main_MiSTer gamecontroller_db.cpp:198,207-217
        void get_ctrl_index_maps(int dev_fd, char *guid, uint16_t *btn_map, ...)
        ...
        if (ioctl(dev_fd, EVIOCGBIT(EV_KEY, sizeof(keybits)), keybits) >= 0)
                for (int i = BTN_JOYSTICK; i < KEY_MAX; i++)
                        if (test_bit(i, keybits)) { btn_map[btn_cnt] = i; btn_cnt++; }

-- so the shipped gamecontrollerdb.txt "platform:MiSTer" PS5 rows
(guide:b11, leftshoulder:b5, back:b9, start:b10) are written for the
BTN_Z-present layout, and the DS4 rows for the BTN_Z-absent one. Declare
it on the wrong device and that device's whole map slides by one: on a
DualSense without it, PS/Home acts as Start and L3 opens the OSD; on a
DualShock 4 with it, Options is read as Guide. Both halves matter, which
is why the capability is declared per-device rather than by adding
BTN_Z to the ps_gamepad_buttons[] table that 6.18 shares with
DualShock 4.

Provenance
----------
Origin:       60e08955fe23c2a1d57834f7dc31860395542e4a
              "dualsense: give mute button and led to system."
              MiSTer-devel/Linux-Kernel_MiSTer, 2021-07-10, against v5.15.
              https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Linux-Kernel_MiSTer/commit/60e08955fe23c2a1d57834f7dc31860395542e4a
Author:       Sorgelig <pour.garbage@gmail.com>
Upstream:     No. v6.18.52 still toggles the mic in-kernel
              (hid-playstation.c: last_btn_mic_state) with no BTN_Z and no
              writable mute LED. patch-provenance.md's original Class-C
              "drop" grouping for this commit was the canary
              misclassification that motivated the full reconciliation
              (docs/kernel-recon, sonnet-verified).
Forward-port: 5.15 -> 6.18.38, Michael C. Ferguson, 2026-07-15, kernel patch
              reconciliation carry decision. BTN_Z capability is declared
              per-device instead of editing the ps_gamepad_buttons[] table,
              which 6.18 shares with DualShock 4 (the fork's 5.15 table was
              DualSense-only). Mute-LED handler uses 6.18's scoped_guard
              locking and dualsense_schedule_work().
Realigned:    2026-09-21, fork-sync increment (docs/kernel-recon/
              fork-sync-2026-09-21.md; record
              docs/kernel-recon/records/0b2ffdd1d13b3a1b92b6732ed04366e06866ea33.json).
              The fork hit the DualShock-4 half of the problem above and
              fixed it in 0b2ffdd1d ("HID: playstation: restrict mute
              button capability to DualSense (#107)", PR #107, Porkchop
              Express) -- arriving at this patch's per-device conclusion
              from the opposite direction, after shipping the shared-table
              form since its 6.18 port. This patch's declaration was moved
              to the shape that merged there: a `bool has_mute_button`
              parameter on ps_gamepad_create(), true for DualSense and
              false for DualShock 4.
              WHY IT IS NOT COSMETIC. The previous form called
              input_set_capability() on ds->gamepad AFTER
              ps_gamepad_create() returned -- i.e. after that function's
              own input_register_device() (linux-6.18.52
              drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c:783). evdev reads the bitmap
              live at EVIOCGBIT, so Main_MiSTer was unaffected and the
              hardware verification of the old form still stands; joydev
              does NOT. joydev_connect() snapshots dev->keybit into its
              keymap/keypam when the handler attaches, which happens
              inside input_register_device() (6.18.52
              drivers/input/joydev.c, `for (i = BTN_JOYSTICK - BTN_MISC;
              i < KEY_MAX - BTN_MISC + 1; i++) if (test_bit(i + BTN_MISC,
              dev->keybit))`), so with the old ordering /dev/input/jsN on
              a DualSense reported 13 buttons and no BTN_Z where stock
              5.15 reported 14. CONFIG_INPUT_JOYDEV=y
              (board/mister/de10nano/linux.config:344), so that interface
              ships. Declaring the capability before registration closes
              it.
              MEASURED identity: with this patch applied to a pristine
              linux-6.18.52 tree, ps_gamepad_create() and
              ps_gamepad_buttons[] diff EMPTY against
              `git show 0b2ffdd1d:drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c`, and both
              call sites match. The EV_KEY bitmap is unchanged on every
              pad -- DualSense keeps BTN_Z, DualShock 4 never had it here
              -- so no gamecontrollerdb `bN` index moves for any device.
KEEP IN
LOCKSTEP:     board/mister/de10nano/linux-patches-beta/0037-*.patch is a
              7.x-re-anchored copy of this file (7.x inserts the DualSense
              Edge paddle blocks at two of these anchors) and
              board/mister/de25nano/linux-patches/0037-*.patch symlinks to
              that copy. The added lines are byte-identical between the
              two; edit both or neither.

Signed-off-by: Sorgelig <pour.garbage@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c | 64 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@
 	/* Microphone */
 	bool update_mic_mute;
 	bool mic_muted;
-	bool last_btn_mic_state;
+	struct led_classdev mute_led;
 
 	/* Player leds */
 	bool update_player_leds;
@@ -742,7 +742,7 @@
 }
 
 static struct input_dev *
-ps_gamepad_create(struct hid_device *hdev,
+ps_gamepad_create(struct hid_device *hdev, bool has_mute_button,
 		  int (*play_effect)(struct input_dev *, void *, struct ff_effect *))
 {
 	struct input_dev *gamepad;
@@ -771,6 +771,10 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ps_gamepad_buttons); i++)
 		input_set_capability(gamepad, EV_KEY, ps_gamepad_buttons[i]);
 
+	/* The microphone mute button exists only on DualSense. */
+	if (has_mute_button)
+		input_set_capability(gamepad, EV_KEY, BTN_Z);
+
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PLAYSTATION_FF)
 	if (play_effect) {
 		input_set_capability(gamepad, EV_FF, FF_RUMBLE);
@@ -1404,7 +1408,6 @@
 	u8 battery_data, battery_capacity, charging_status, value;
 	int battery_status;
 	u32 sensor_timestamp;
-	bool btn_mic_state;
 	int i;
 
 	/*
@@ -1457,24 +1460,14 @@
 	input_report_key(ds->gamepad, BTN_THUMBL, ds_report->buttons[1] & DS_BUTTONS1_L3);
 	input_report_key(ds->gamepad, BTN_THUMBR, ds_report->buttons[1] & DS_BUTTONS1_R3);
 	input_report_key(ds->gamepad, BTN_MODE,   ds_report->buttons[2] & DS_BUTTONS2_PS_HOME);
-	input_sync(ds->gamepad);
-
 	/*
-	 * The DualSense has an internal microphone, which can be muted through a mute button
-	 * on the device. The driver is expected to read the button state and program the device
-	 * to mute/unmute audio at the hardware level.
+	 * Stock MiSTer reports the mic-mute button to userspace as BTN_Z
+	 * (an extra mappable button) instead of toggling the microphone
+	 * in-kernel; the mute LED is owned by userspace via the ":mute"
+	 * LED class device registered in dualsense_create().
 	 */
-	btn_mic_state = !!(ds_report->buttons[2] & DS_BUTTONS2_MIC_MUTE);
-	if (btn_mic_state && !ds->last_btn_mic_state) {
-		scoped_guard(spinlock_irqsave, &ps_dev->lock) {
-			ds->update_mic_mute = true;
-			ds->mic_muted = !ds->mic_muted; /* toggle */
-		}
-
-		/* Schedule updating of microphone state at hardware level. */
-		dualsense_schedule_work(ds);
-	}
-	ds->last_btn_mic_state = btn_mic_state;
+	input_report_key(ds->gamepad, BTN_Z, ds_report->buttons[2] & DS_BUTTONS2_MIC_MUTE);
+	input_sync(ds->gamepad);
 
 	/*
 	 * Parse HP/MIC plugged state data for USB use case, since Bluetooth
@@ -1699,6 +1692,20 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int dualsense_mute_led_set_brightness(struct led_classdev *led,
+					     enum led_brightness brightness)
+{
+	struct hid_device *hdev = to_hid_device(led->dev->parent);
+	struct dualsense *ds = hid_get_drvdata(hdev);
+
+	scoped_guard(spinlock_irqsave, &ds->base.lock) {
+		ds->update_mic_mute = true;
+		ds->mic_muted = !!brightness;
+	}
+	dualsense_schedule_work(ds);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static struct ps_device *dualsense_create(struct hid_device *hdev)
 {
 	struct dualsense *ds;
@@ -1770,7 +1777,7 @@
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	ds->gamepad = ps_gamepad_create(hdev, dualsense_play_effect);
+	ds->gamepad = ps_gamepad_create(hdev, true, dualsense_play_effect);
 	if (IS_ERR(ds->gamepad)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(ds->gamepad);
 		goto err;
@@ -1839,6 +1846,21 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto err;
 
+	/* Mute button LED, owned by userspace like on stock MiSTer. */
+	ds->mute_led.name = devm_kasprintf(&hdev->dev, GFP_KERNEL, "%s:mute",
+					   dev_name(&hdev->dev));
+	if (!ds->mute_led.name) {
+		ret = -ENOMEM;
+		goto err;
+	}
+	ds->mute_led.brightness = 0;
+	ds->mute_led.max_brightness = 1;
+	ds->mute_led.brightness_set_blocking = dualsense_mute_led_set_brightness;
+	ds->mute_led.flags = LED_CORE_SUSPENDRESUME | LED_HW_PLUGGABLE;
+	ret = devm_led_classdev_register(&hdev->dev, &ds->mute_led);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err;
+
 	ret = ps_device_set_player_id(ps_dev);
 	if (ret) {
 		hid_err(hdev, "Failed to assign player id for DualSense: %d\n", ret);
@@ -2762,7 +2784,7 @@
 		hid_warn(hdev, "Gyroscope and accelerometer will be inaccurate.\n");
 	}
 
-	ds4->gamepad = ps_gamepad_create(hdev, dualshock4_play_effect);
+	ds4->gamepad = ps_gamepad_create(hdev, false, dualshock4_play_effect);
 	if (IS_ERR(ds4->gamepad)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(ds4->gamepad);
 		goto err;
